  "report_impact_coverage": [
    {
      "impact_id": "retroactive_claim",
      "evidence": [
        "Killed and Revived Gauges Retroactively Claim Rewards from Inactive Periods",
        "[GaugeManager.killGauge()](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-10-hybra-finance/blob/66c42f3c9754f1b38942c69ebc0d3e4c0f8fdeb2/ve33/contracts/GaugeManager.sol#L408-L423) and [GaugeManager.reviveGauge()](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-10-hybra-finance/blob/66c42f3c9754f1b38942c69ebc0d3e4c0f8fdeb2/ve33/contracts/GaugeManager.sol#L428-L433) functions fail to synchronize the gauge-specific `supplyIndex[_gauge]` with the global `index` accumulator. When a gauge is killed, its `supplyIndex` remains frozen at the pre-kill value. Upon revival, this stale checkpoint allows the gauge to retroactively claim all rewards that accrued during its inactive period through the [_updateForAfterDistribution()",
        "Without resetting `supplyIndex` to the current `index`, a revived gauge inherits the stale checkpoint from before it was killed, making it eligible to claim rewards it never earned."
      ],
      "claim_ids": [
        "impact_claim_retroactive_claim_c9246ec7"
      ],
      "status": "formalized",
      "reason": "Program-generated exact coverage for selected direct impact."
    },
    {
      "impact_id": "unearned_rewards",
      "evidence": [
        "Without resetting `supplyIndex` to the current `index`, a revived gauge inherits the stale checkpoint from before it was killed, making it eligible to claim rewards it never earned.",
        "The gauge received rewards for 2 epochs that occurred before it was killed, which it should never be able to claim after revival."
      ],
      "claim_ids": [
        "impact_claim_unearned_rewards_be74f5b8"
      ],
      "status": "formalized",
      "reason": "Program-generated exact coverage for selected direct impact."
